instructions:
Implement the game lifecycle in game-core/src/engine/game.ts (NO classes, NO mutation). This is the last pure-engine module: it BUILDS the initial GameState from card data (setup), runs the start-of-turn routine (startTurn), and decides when the game ends and who wins (checkWin). It REUSES the existing modules — do NOT reimplement shuffles, draws, market building, revive, or seat advancement.

Imports (exact):
```ts
import type { GameSetup, GameState, PlayerState, CardDef, Prompt } from '../types';
import { makeRng, shuffle, nextInt } from '../util/rng';
import { draw } from './deck';
import { buildMarket } from './market';
import { revive } from './characters';
import { advanceTurn } from './turn';
```
(market.buildMarket takes `ReadonlyArray<{ pileId: string; instanceIds: readonly string[] }>` and returns `Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>` — you must convert that to GameState's `marketPiles` shape `Record<string, MarketPile>` where MarketPile = `{ pileId: string; cards: readonly string[] }`.)

STYLE RULES: strict TypeScript with noUncheckedIndexedAccess. No `any`. No default exports. Never mutate inputs — NEW state, copied arrays. Export ONLY these three functions.

GLOBAL instance-id scheme used by setup (spell it exactly): for any CardDef `d`, its copies are the instance ids `${d.id}#1`, `${d.id}#2`, ..., `${d.id}#${d.copies}`. Every instance ever created must also be registered in the returned state's `cards` record: `{ instanceId, cardId: d.id, location: { zone: 'mansionDeck', index: 0 } }` (location is not heavily used yet; set a plausible zone). The state's `cardDefs` record maps every card's `id` -> its CardDef.

----------------- export function setup(setup: GameSetup, cards: ReadonlyArray<CardDef>, piles: ReadonlyArray<{ pileId: string; cardIds: readonly string[] }>): GameState

Build the full initial state. Algorithm (in order):

1. const defsById = new Map(cards.map(c => [c.id, c])). const cardDefs = Object.fromEntries(cards.map(c => [c.id, c])).
2. let rng = makeRng(setup.seed). Helper: const rngShuffle = (items: readonly string[]): readonly string[] => { const r = shuffle(rng, items); rng = r.rng; return r.value; }. Helper pickChar(ids): const i = nextInt(rng, ids.length); rng = i.rng; return ids[i.value]. (Use an index-into-array via nextInt as described.)
3. Seats: for each player spec p (index i) in setup.players: build a PlayerState:
   - characterCardId: p.characterCardId if provided; else pick one from the type-'character' defs (their ids, in `cards` order) using pickChar (call once per seat, numbering duplicates like 'ch-1#1' if two seats pick the same id).
   - characterInstanceId = `${characterCardId}#${i+1}` (seat-unique). Register it in cards with cardId characterCardId.
   - hp = maxHp = defsById.get(characterCardId).maxHp; decorations 0; level 1; downed false; dead false; controller/botLevel from the spec; name p.name.
   - pools: turnAmmo 0, turnGold 0, actionsLeft 1, buysLeft 1, exploresLeft 1, weaponDamageBonusThisTurn 0.
   - Starting deck (rulebook 'First Timer'): 7 instances of the ammunition card whose id starts with 'am-1' (from cards), 1 instance of the 'we-1' (Handgun) def, 2 instances of the 'we-4' (Combat Knife) def — SKIP any id that is not present in `cards` (tests will include all three). instance ids follow the global scheme (`am-1#1`..`am-1#7`, `we-1#1`, `we-4#1`, `we-4#2`). Set inventory = rngShuffle([all 10 ids]) AFTER registering every one in the cards record; discard []; hand = []; playArea []; attached [].
   - seats[i] = that PlayerState.
4. Recycle the mansion pile: mansionCardIds = cards.filter(d => d.type === 'infected' || d.type === 'token' || (d.type === 'item' && d.id === 'it-3')).flatMap making ALL instance ids (copies), then mansionDeck = rngShuffle(ids). Register each in cards. mansionBottom = []. (Yellow Herb = 'it-3'.)
5. Market piles: for each pileSpec in piles: collect all instance ids for every cardId in pileSpec.cardIds (all copies), make ONE combined array, then pile cards = rngShuffle(combined). Register each instance in cards. marketPiles = { [pileId]: { pileId, cards } }. (Test fixtures give one pile per weapon or combined piles — follow the spec input literally.)
6. Draw opening hands: for each seat i: d = draw({ deck: seats[i].inventory, discard: [], reshuffledDiscard: [], count: 5 }); seats[i] = { ...seats[i], inventory: d.deck, hand: d.hand }.
7. Initial pools already set in step 3 (1/1/1, 0/0/0).
8. Return GameState: { version: 1, seed: setup.seed, rngState: rng.s, phase: 'main', activeSeat: 0, turnNumber: 1, seats, marketPiles (converted: each pile `{ pileId, cards }`), mansionDeck, mansionBottom, removed: [], cards (record of all registered instances), cardDefs, prompts: [], winners: [], log: [] }.

NOTE on zone values in CardInstance.location: any plausible zone string from the CardZone union is fine ('hand' for dealt/private, 'marketPile' with pileId for market instances, 'mansionDeck' for mansion instances) — correctness of exact per-instance location is not asserted; PRESENCE and cardId are.

----------------- export function startTurn(state: GameState): GameState

Begin the active player's turn. Guard: if state.phase !== 'main' return state unchanged.

1. player = state.seats[state.activeSeat] (cast as PlayerState; state built by setup so it exists).
2. If player.downed:
   - ch = revive({ hp: player.hp, maxHp: player.maxHp, decorations: player.decorations, level: player.level, downed: player.downed, dead: player.dead, hand: player.hand, discard: player.discard, inventory: player.inventory }) — characters.revive returns the reduced CharacterState (it lowers maxHp by 20, sets hp = new max, clears downed, or marks dead when maxHp <= 0).
   - Then the recovering player draws 5: d = draw({ deck: ch.inventory, discard: ch.discard, reshuffledDiscard: [], count: 5 }) (fixture inventories are big enough; no reshuffle path needed).
   - NewPlayer = { ...player, hp: ch.hp, maxHp: ch.maxHp, downed: ch.downed, dead: ch.dead, hand: d.hand, inventory: d.deck, discard: d.discard, playArea: [], turnAmmo: 0, turnGold: 0, actionsLeft: 1, buysLeft: 1, exploresLeft: 1, weaponDamageBonusThisTurn: 0 }.
   - The recovering player SKIPS their turn: ctx = advanceTurn({ seatCount: state.seats.length, activeSeat: state.activeSeat, turnNumber: state.turnNumber, aliveSeats: state.seats.map((s,i) => s.dead ? -1 : i).filter(i => i >= 0) }); activeSeat = ctx.activeSeat; turnNumber = ctx.turnNumber. (If the revive killed them — ch.dead true — they are not in aliveSeats, so advance skips them.)
3. Else (not downed): NewPlayer = { ...player, turnAmmo: 0, turnGold: 0, actionsLeft: 1, buysLeft: 1, exploresLeft: 1, weaponDamageBonusThisTurn: 0, playArea: [] } (clear the play area per 'end of turn' cleanup happens here in v1). activeSeat/turnNumber unchanged.
4. Return { ...state, version: state.version + 1, seats: seats.map(..., replaced for active), activeSeat, turnNumber }. Log is NOT touched (startTurn is engine-side, not an Action in v1).

----------------- export function checkWin(state: GameState): { gameOver: boolean; winners: readonly number[]; endReason?: 'uroborosDefeated' | 'allPlayersDead' }

1. uroborosDefeated: any seat (index i) whose attached contains an instanceId whose cardDef (state.cardDefs[state.cards[instanceId].cardId]) has infectedEffects with kind 'shuffleBackIfNotDefeated' (Uroboros Aheri). When true: gameOver true; endReason 'uroborosDefeated'; winners = seats sorted by (decorations desc, then hp desc), taking ALL seats that tie with the top (max decorations; among those, all with the top hp — so exact tie = both listed). Return that.
2. else all dead: every seat dead -> gameOver true, winners [], endReason 'allPlayersDead'. A state with ZERO seats (empty seats array) also counts as all dead.
3. else: gameOver false, winners [].

