11. startTurn downed death: s = setup2(1); dying = { ...s, seats: s.seats.map((p,i) => i===0 ? { ...p, downed: true, hp: 0, maxHp: 15, hand: [], inventory: [], discard: [] } : p) }; t = startTurn(dying) -> t.seats[0].dead true; downed false; maxHp -5; activeSeat 1; turnNumber 2 (advanced past the dead seat).
12. startTurn not in main phase: setup-phase state { ...s, phase: 'setup' } -> startTurn returns the SAME values (result.phase 'setup', version 1 — i.e. unchanged behavior: assert result.version === 1 and result.phase === 'setup' and result.seats === s.seats toBe).
13. checkWin not over: setup2(1) -> { gameOver: false, winners: [] }.
14. checkWin uroboros: s = setup2(1); won = { ...s, seats: s.seats.map((p,i) => i===0 ? { ...p, attached: ['ma-10#1'] } : p) }; c = checkWin(won) -> gameOver true; endReason 'uroborosDefeated'; winners [0].
15. checkWin uroboros decides by decorations: won with seat0 attached ['ma-10#1'] decorations 3, seat1 attached ['ma-10#2'] decorations 5 -> winners [1] (higher decorations wins).
16. checkWin uroboros tie-break hp: both seats attached, decorations equal (set both 4), seat0 hp 70 seat1 hp 60 -> winners [0] (higher hp).
17. checkWin uroboros exact tie: both attached, decorations 4, hp 70 -> winners [0,1] (shared win).
18. checkWin all dead: dead = { ...setup2(1), seats: setup2(1).seats.map(p => ({ ...p, dead: true })) }; c = checkWin(dead) -> gameOver true; endReason 'allPlayersDead'; winners [].
19. checkWin one dead one alive: seats[0] dead true -> gameOver false.
20. checkWin empty seats: { ...setup2(1), seats: [] } -> gameOver true; endReason 'allPlayersDead'.

